winex11: Manage owned windows that are neither popups nor topmost.

is_window_managed() leaves a window unmanaged (override-redirect) when it
is shown without activation and has no caption, frame, popup system menu,
WS_EX_APPWINDOW or owned popups. A borderless WPF window owned by the main
window, such as Affinity's sub-tool panel, is exactly that. KWin on Wayland
keeps override-redirect windows above every window, so the panel stayed
above other applications after the user switched to them. On Windows an
owned window that is not topmost stays above its owner and goes behind
other applications with it, which only the window manager can do. Manage
such windows; popups (menus, tooltips, WPF popups) and topmost windows stay
unmanaged.

Also leave owned windows without a caption out of the pager and of KDE's
window switcher, as Windows leaves owned windows out of Alt-Tab: managed,
the panel had become an Alt-Tab entry of its own. Owned dialogs keep their
entry.

With a native Wayland window activated over it, the panel is covered;
before, it stayed on top. KWin sees it as a transient of the main window,
in the normal layer, at the position Affinity gives it.

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index f1ed029..b3bb8c3 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -464,6 +464,11 @@ static BOOL is_window_managed( HWND hwnd, UINT swp_flags, BOOL fullscreen )
     if (ex_style & WS_EX_APPWINDOW) return TRUE;
     /* windows that own popups are managed */
     if (has_owned_popups( hwnd )) return TRUE;
+    /* owned windows that are neither popups nor topmost are managed: they
+     * belong above their owner and below other applications' windows, and
+     * only the window manager can keep them there. An unmanaged window stays
+     * above every window, under KWin on Wayland at least. */
+    if (!(style & WS_POPUP) && !(ex_style & WS_EX_TOPMOST) && NtUserGetWindowRelative( hwnd, GW_OWNER )) return TRUE;
     /* default: not managed */
     return FALSE;
 }
@@ -1540,7 +1545,13 @@ static void update_net_wm_states( struct x11drv_win_data *data )
             || (ex_style & WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW && !(ex_style & WS_EX_APPWINDOW)))
             new_state |= (1 << NET_WM_STATE_SKIP_TASKBAR) | (1 << NET_WM_STATE_SKIP_PAGER) | (1 << KDE_NET_WM_STATE_SKIP_SWITCHER);
         else if (!(ex_style & WS_EX_APPWINDOW) && NtUserGetWindowRelative( data->hwnd, GW_OWNER ))
+        {
             new_state |= (1 << NET_WM_STATE_SKIP_TASKBAR);
+            /* an owned window without a caption is a panel or palette, which
+             * Windows leaves out of Alt-Tab; owned dialogs stay in it */
+            if ((style & WS_CAPTION) != WS_CAPTION)
+                new_state |= (1 << NET_WM_STATE_SKIP_PAGER) | (1 << KDE_NET_WM_STATE_SKIP_SWITCHER);
+        }
     }
 
     window_set_net_wm_state( data, new_state );
